<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 76,624 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 76,624 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 76,624 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Friday compared to 56,778 tonnes in the same period on Thursday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Friday	June 5</p>
<p>    Export cargo		25,346	 9,146</p>
<p>    Import cargo		51,278	47,632</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, four ships sailed and five berthed. In the next 24 hours, five are expected to sail and five are expected to arrive.</p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	Tonnes/TEUs  Ship			Berthing</p>
<p>Gas oil		60,000	 New Tatina		 7/6</p>
<p>Palm oil		9,000	 Jian She-32		7/6</p>
<p>Vehicles		  100	 Hual Margarita	   7/7</p>
<p>Palm oil	     10,000	 Wawasan Courage	 10/6</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
